.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt MOUSE 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mouse
.Nd PS/2 mouse input driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "device mouse"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver handles IRQ12 input from the PS/2 auxiliary device path.
It consumes standard 3-byte PS/2 mouse packets from port
.Li 0x60 ,
maintains cumulative X/Y state, queues relative motion events, and forwards
movement/button changes into the kernel input-event stream.
.Pp
The current implementation supports:
.Bl -bullet
.It
standard 3-byte PS/2 packets
.It
packet realignment by discarding malformed first bytes until byte 0 bit 3 is set
.It
overflow clamping to
.Li +/-255
per axis when packet overflow bits are set
.It
button reporting for left, right, and middle buttons
.El
.Pp
Each completed packet emits relative-axis events for
.Dv REL_X
and
.Dv REL_Y ,
button events for
.Dv BTN_LEFT ,
.Dv BTN_RIGHT ,
and
.Dv BTN_MIDDLE ,
then an
.Dv EV_SYN
boundary marker.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/sys/drivers/input/mouse.c"
.It Pa /sys/drivers/input/mouse.c
Driver implementation.
.It Pa /sys/drivers/input/mouse.h
Driver interface.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ps2 4 ,
.Xr keyboard 4
